# Aston Martin DB Mk III fixed-head coupe, 1957-1959.
#
# The final development of the DB2/4 line: the 2+2 fixed-head coupe with the
# hatchback tailgate, the tall mesh grille, the projecting bonnet scoop and the
# side vent behind the front wheel. 551 built before the DB4 replaced it. The
# drophead and the two-seat coupe are not modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_DB_Mark_III
#
# Dimensions 4.369 x 1.651 x 1.359 m, wheelbase 2.515 m (172 x 65 x 53.5 in,
# 99 in). The hull measures 4.369 m on the 2.515 m wheelbase.
#
# Shape reference: one black 1958 car, plate VD 40052, photographed at Morges in
# 2013. Image 1 is a true level side elevation and governs the flank and roof
# line; image 2 the mesh grille, lamps and bonnet scoop; image 3 the hatchback
# tail, fins and vertical rear lamps. The grille is modelled as the fine mesh
# with horizontal and vertical wires that image 2 shows, not as vertical bars.
#
# Colours: no British-market colour list was found (grade d); cars of this era
# were finished to order, so the objects carry plain names: British Racing
# Green, silver, black and red. Weights green 3, silver 3, black 2, red 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 235 km/h, the quoted maximum of the 3.0-litre six. Comfort 60/270, on the
# line 180 + 1.5 x 60: the same open, low-roofed 2+2 as the DB5. Classes 3,4.
#
# Dates are road presence: 1957 intro, retires staggered 1975-1978 on an
# eighteen- to twenty-one-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-db-mk3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-db-mk3.dae (77 objects). References:
# citycars/references/aston-db-mk3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the side-window pillars lean more than the photographed
# car's, and the hatch glazing edge stands slightly proud of the roofline in
# profile. Uniform scaling of the side photograph by its overall length implies
# a 2.73 m wheelbase and 1.41 m height against the published 2.515 m and
# 1.359 m; the build keeps the published figures and attributes the difference
# to close-camera perspective. At 128 px the long bonnet, fastback roof, mesh
# grille, side vent and fins read as a DB Mk III.

obj=citycar
name=AstonDBMkIII(BritishRacingGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1957
intro_month=1
retire_year=1978
retire_month=6
speed=235
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=60
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=270

Image[E]=./images/aston-db-mk3-britishracinggreen_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/aston-db-mk3-britishracinggreen_SE.0.0,-13,0
Image[S]=./images/aston-db-mk3-britishracinggreen_S.0.0,0,0
Image[SW]=./images/aston-db-mk3-britishracinggreen_SW.0.0,-8,10
Image[W]=./images/aston-db-mk3-britishracinggreen_W.0.0,4,5
Image[NW]=./images/aston-db-mk3-britishracinggreen_NW.0.0,12,10
Image[N]=./images/aston-db-mk3-britishracinggreen_N.0.0,0,33
